SWEET PMIC SRC print (patch 0318, ALL-ON tracker T-02/T-24, docs/research/139-gs101-bcl-brownout.md, review 0316). Log only, no hardware access, no new bus traffic: bsd/dev/sweet_chg_i2c.c prints the S2MPG10 / S2MPG11 reset-source latches that the shim read (shim/pmicsrc.c, `--pmic-src`; READ-ONLY ACPM FUNC_READ of STATUS1/STATUS2/PWRONSRC/OFFSRC and S2MPG11 STATUS1/OFFSRC, nothing cleared) and handed over as boot-args, because the shim console never reaches the host in a --boot-xnu boot (same route as --mif-clk / patch 0214). Boot-args (hex via PE_parse_boot_argn, pexpert/gen/bootargs.c getval, same as debug=0xBAADF00D): sweetps10=0xAABBCCDD (S2MPG10 STATUS1,STATUS2,PWRONSRC,OFFSRC, MSB first, present only when all four were read), sweetps11=0xAABB (S2MPG11 STATUS1,OFFSRC, present only when both were read), sweetpsrc=N (0 all six read; 1..6 the read of register index N-1 failed and the later ones were skipped; 7 an ACPM gate refused). Where patch 0314 printed the two `SWEET PMIC GAP: s2mpg10|s2mpg11 ... no read path` lines (P2 group 4, i2c_g_chg), a kernel that finds any of the three boot-args prints instead `SWEET PMIC SRC: s2mpg10 STATUS1=0x.. STATUS2=0x.. PWRONSRC=0x.. OFFSRC=0x.. s2mpg11 STATUS1=0x.. OFFSRC=0x.. rc=N (read by the shim, not cleared)` (a register with no value prints ERR, never a made-up one), a GAP line for rc != 0 or a missing sweetpsrc, and one GAP line that INT1..INT6 stay unread (clear-on-read). No sweetps* boot-arg (shim without --pmic-src): the 0314 GAP lines exactly as before. Bit meaning of PWRONSRC / OFFSRC is not public (research 139 section 2): printed raw. Applies after 0314. Host test: shim/pmicsrc_host_test.c (token format), kernel string check: tools/build-xnu-image.sh refuses --pmic-src without 'sweetps10' in the kernel. Not run on hardware.

